tantale: copyright and licences of bundled third-party files
============================================================

tantale's own code is distributed under the MIT licence (files LICENSE
and LICENSE.md, copyright the tantale authors). The package also
bundles programs and data written by others, and tantale_setup()
downloads more of them, listed below. They are not covered by the MIT
licence: each keeps its own terms. The paths of bundled files are those
of the source package; in an installed package, drop the leading
"inst/".


1. AnnoTALE, PrediTALE and TALEcorrection (Jstacs)
--------------------------------------------------

Not part of the package. tantale_setup(install = TRUE) downloads them
in the archive tantale-tools-1.tar.gz, attached to the release tools-1
of https://github.com/scunnac/tantale, which holds:
  AnnoTALEcli-1.5.jar
      AnnoTALE 1.5, command-line version
      sha256 fe99d084073343a7018226e221b0bf291af92300c9f6f1bb701bd0923e32e135
      upstream https://www.jstacs.de/downloads/AnnoTALEcli-1.5.jar
  PrediTALE.jar
      sha256 67a3ef81c2badbd635a7dca6ecba3ec65a773ca7eae05d70aeab09275d654a21
      upstream https://www.jstacs.de/downloads/PrediTALE.jar
  talecorrect/TALEcorrection.jar
      sha256 9adf9de20a41caa21bc0e93946cdf3802d1d83ed77476eca856a95a2d9383312
      upstream https://www.jstacs.de/downloads/TALECorrection_scripts.zip
  talecorrect/ (the other files: HMMs/, *.java, *.sh,
      TALEcorrection.xml), which accompany TALEcorrection.
  LICENSES/COPYING.GPL-3, README.md, MANIFEST.

Each jar is an unmodified copy of its upstream file, and the HMMs are
identical to those in the zip archive above (checked by sha256,
2026-09-23).

Copyright: the Jstacs authors (https://www.jstacs.de).

Licence: GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any
later version. The full text is in the archive's LICENSES/COPYING.GPL-3,
identical to the COPYING.txt file inside each jar.

Source code: the jars contain compiled classes only. Their source is
part of the Jstacs project, https://github.com/Jstacs/Jstacs:
  projects/xanthogenomes/  (AnnoTALE)
  projects/tals/prediction/  (PrediTALE)
  projects/talecorrect/  (TALEcorrection)

The jars also contain third-party Java libraries (BioJava, Colt, Jama,
the Rserve client, Apache libraries and others), under their own
licences; the licence and notice files that came with them are inside
each jar (META-INF/ and the jar root).

References:
  AnnoTALE: Grau J. et al. (2016). Scientific Reports 6, 21077.
    https://doi.org/10.1038/srep21077
  PrediTALE: Erkes A. et al. (2019). PLoS Computational Biology 15,
